    {
      "id": "claim_6d0dc80e30aa437596ff9943a7bd1d94",
      "statement": "Silhouette, Davies-Bouldin and Calinski-Harabasz are computed only over assigned points with noise excluded and are left undefined when fewer than two clusters survive, while DBCV is computed across the whole labelling.",
